perturbations.a:
Select2: How to stop tags arrangement  

When user chooses many items (tags), they are automatically organized alphabetically. How to stop automatic arrangement and maintain user's sequence using Select2 4.0?  

Update:  

The stated "possible duplicate inquiry" is for the older version of Select2 v3... I ask about version 4... It varies from older ones and stated answers doesn't resolve the issue.  

I've found a resolution that functions with Select2 v4. It alters the sequence of items - items selected by user are shifted to the end.  

$("select").select2();  

$("select").on("select2:select", function (evt) {  
  var element = evt.params.data.element;  
  var $element = $(element);  

  $element detach();  
  $(this).append($element);  
  $(this).trigger("change");  
});  
<link href="//cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/select2/4.0.0/css/select2.css" rel="stylesheet"/>  

<script src="//cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery/2.1.3/jquery.js"></script>  
<script src="//cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/select2/4.0.0/js/select2.js"></script>  

<select style="width: 500px;" multiple="multiple">  
  <option>two</option>  
  <option>four</option>  
  <option>six</option>  
</select>  

Update  

The resolution was located here: github.com/select2/select2/issues/3106. Its creator is kevin-brown.

