perturbations.a:
Laravel 5 Form request validation with arguments  

I am utilizing form request validation and there are some rules that requires external values as a arguments.  

Here are my validation rules for modifying a business profile inside a form request class,  

public function rules()  
{  
    return [  
        'name' => 'needed|unique:businesses,name,'.$business->id,  
        'url' => 'needed|url|unique:businesses'  
    ];  
}  

I can utilize this on the controller by type hinting it.  

public function postBusinessEdit(BusinessEditRequest $request, Business $business)  
{  
    //  
}  

But how to forward the $business object as a argument to the rules method?  

Lets say this is your model binding:  

$router->model('business', 'App\Business');  

Then you can reference the Business class from inside the FormRequest object like this:  

public function rules()  
{  
    $business = $this->route()->getParameter('business');  
    // rest of the code  
}  

Note that if you utilize your form request both for create and refresh validation, while creating the record, the business variable will be null because your object does not exist yet. So take care to perform the needed checks before referencing the object properties or methods.

