perturbations.a:
SASS, Rails 3.1: Loading stylesheets in vendor/assets

I'm utilizing SASS to load stylesheets in a Rails 3.1(sass-rails 3.1) application. For instance, sass partials in app/assets/stylesheets are loaded using @import in application.sass -

 @import "pages/common"
 @import "pages/**/*"
 @import "jquery-ui.css"

Now, I additionally want to load vendor/assets/stylesheets. Note that I'm not utilizing require vendor, as @import pages/* seems to be the sass recommended method of doing it. Files here will be css, and not sass or scss. I cannot utilize @import ../../../vendor/assets/stylesheets/* as it functions only for sass and scss files.

Is there any method of doing this ?

Update

What I possess now is this.

application.css.scss

//= require_tree .
//= require vendor
//= require_self

This encompasses all the sass partials mentioned above. The require vendor in

vendor/assets/stylesheets/vendor.css appears like

//= require_tree .

A caveat of this method is that sass mixins(user defined & plugins) and common variables are not accessible in all partials. What I possess now is a _common_imports.sass which I @import first thing in all partials.

common_imports.sass

@import "colors"
@import "compass/css3/gradient"
@import "compass/css3/border-radius"
@import "compass/css3/box-shadow"

Importing common_imports in all partials feels very repetitive.

If I'm comprehending you correctly, I believe this might assist.

Add the following to config/application.rb, inside the class Application < Rails::Application block:

config.sass.load_paths << File expand_path('../../lib/assets/stylesheets/')
config.sass.load_paths << File expand_path('../../vendor/assets/stylesheets/')

I've just added the above to an application, and the following directives are now both functioning:

  • Import Sass:
    @import 'grid' in app/assets/stylesheets/application.css.scss locates the file vendor/assets/stylesheets/_grid.scss;
  • Import standard CSS:
    @import 'background', again in application.css.scss, locates vendor/assets/stylesheets/background.css.

Does that assist? Sorry if I've misinterpreted the issue!

